# Docs Reading Guide

Start here before reading longer docs.

{{ project_name }} uses progressive disclosure for repository knowledge: this file is the entry point, specs describe current intended behavior, decisions explain why major choices were made, and tasks describe repeatable maintenance workflows.

For each project session, read these docs first:

1. [{{ main_spec_title }}](./specs/{{ main_spec_slug }}-v0.1.md) - Product scope, target user, current behavior, non-goals, and validation strategy.
2. [Architecture Layering v0.1](./specs/architecture-layering-v0.1.md) - Dependency direction, ownership boundaries, and current enforcement.
3. [Agent Governance v0.1](./specs/agent-governance-v0.1.md) - Repository harness, comment policy, generated artifacts, and validation principles.

When changing project conventions, validation scripts, architecture rules, generated schemas, or agent-facing docs, read [Agent Governance v0.1](./specs/agent-governance-v0.1.md).

When changing specs, decisions, generated contracts, or code, keep the affected artifacts aligned in the same change. If that is not feasible, leave an explicit follow-up.

When checking whether docs, generated contracts, scripts, and code still align, use [Alignment Check Task](./tasks/alignment-check.md).

Before marking local implementation work complete, run `./scripts/validate-changed-scope.mjs`. Use `./scripts/finalize.sh` for CI, pre-merge, or explicit full finalization.

Before scaffolding a backend, frontend, feature slice, or validation gate, use [Scaffold Planning Task](./tasks/scaffold-planning.md).

When backend API shapes change, use [Schema Generation Task](./tasks/schema-generation.md).
{% if frontend_stack != 'none' %}
When a frontend exists, explicitly evaluate Playwright E2E with [E2E Testing Task](./tasks/e2e-testing.md) and [Playwright E2E Impact Tags](./specs/playwright-e2e-impact-tags.md). Enable it when stable user journeys exist; otherwise record the deferral reason.
{% endif %}
